// The constructor frame catalog: English renderings for raw `deckmaste_core`
// constructors, parallel to macro definitions' own `frames:` field
// (`crates/macro_ron/src/set.rs`, `MacroDef.frames`). Canon RON is 83.5% raw
// constructors (`docs/superpowers/research/2026-07-30-macro-frames/
// macro-schema-census.md` §6), so this catalog is most of the lexicon, not
// an appendix.
//
// Loaded by `deckmaste_frames::schema::load_constructor_frames`. Each
// `constructor` names a bare `deckmaste_core` variant (verified against
// `cargo xtask map enums`, not memory — see below); `params` names each
// positional hole's type, in the order the entry's frames reference them
// (`<Param(0)>` is `params[0]`).
//
// Three pilot entries, param names/arities verified against source (all
// deviations from the round's original guess are noted inline):
[
    // `Action::DealDamage(Reference, Count, Reference)` — verified at
    // `crates/deckmaste_core/src/action.rs:145` (`cargo xtask map enums`
    // line 53). The pilot's original third param name, "Target", isn't a
    // real param type; the constructor's third field is a plain `Reference`
    // (the damage's patient object/player), same as the first, so it's
    // corrected to `Reference` here.
    (constructor: "DealDamage", params: ["Reference", "Count", "Reference"],
     frames: ["<Param(0)> deals <Param(1)> damage to <Param(2)>"]),

    // `PlayerAction::GainLife(Count)` (`action.rs:306`, `map enums` line 73)
    // is arity-1 on its own — but a bare `GainLife(N)` in an effect slot
    // never appears un-embedded: `Action::By(#[macro_ron(default =
    // "Reference::You")] Reference, PlayerAction)` carries the
    // `#[macro_ron(embed)]` marker (`action.rs:288-291`), so a RON author's
    // `GainLife(1)` is really `By(Reference::You, GainLife(Count::Literal(1)))`
    // with the subject defaulted. The catalog entry targets that authored
    // surface, not the bare `PlayerAction` variant alone, so `params` stays
    // the round's original `["Reference", "Count"]` (Param(0) = the `By`
    // subject, Param(1) = the count) — no adjustment needed here beyond
    // this note. Declarative for `You`, per the corpus sweep (0 imperative
    // "Gain N life" attestations vs 236 "You gain N life",
    // `docs/superpowers/research/2026-07-30-macro-frames/
    // corpus-alternation.md` §3) — the agreement side table (Task 4) derives
    // gains/gain from the subject filler, so no guard is needed on this
    // pilot entry.
    (constructor: "GainLife", params: ["Reference", "Count"],
     frames: ["<Param(0)> gains <Param(1)> life"]),

    // `TargetSpec::Target(Quantity, Predicate)` (`target_spec.rs:33`, `map
    // enums` line 890) is arity-2 with no default sugar on either field (no
    // `#[macro_ron(...)]` marker on this variant) — unlike `GainLife` above,
    // there is no embed/default path that collapses it to one argument at
    // the RON surface, so the round's original single-`Predicate` params
    // list can't construct a real `Target(...)` value and is corrected to
    // the real two-field signature `["Quantity", "Predicate"]`. The pilot's
    // "target <predicate>" wording (singular: "target creature", not
    // "target N creatures") is preserved by guarding Param(0) (`Quantity`)
    // to the real, sibling-precedented "exactly one" constant — the existing
    // `TargetOne` macro (`plugins/builtin/macros/target/TargetOne.ron`)
    // already invokes exactly `Target(Exactly(1), Param(0))` for the same
    // idiom — and surfacing only Param(1) (`Predicate`) in the frame text.
    (constructor: "Target", params: ["Quantity", "Predicate"],
     frames: [(text: "target <Param(1)>", when: [(0, "Exactly(1)")])]),
]
